174-### Step 2b: Resilience Hooks
175-
176:**PostCompact hook** — long multi-agent audits may trigger context compaction. Configure a PostCompact hook to reinject critical scan state after compaction:
177:- List of dispatched agents and their status (running/completed/failed)
178:- Current finding count per agent
179-- Scan metadata (target path, detected stacks, start time)
180-
181:**StopFailure hook** — if an agent fails due to API error (rate limit, timeout), the StopFailure hook should:
182:1. Log the failure: agent name, error type, turn count at failure
183:2. Retry the agent once with `maxTurns: 10` (reduced scope)
184:3. If retry fails, mark the agent as failed and continue — do NOT block the entire audit
185-
186-### Step 2c: Workflow-Based Orchestration (v2.1.154+)
187-
188:For large monorepos or wide agent fan-outs, the dynamic **Workflow tool** can orchestrate the audit deterministically instead of manual `Agent` dispatch. Author a workflow (or call `Workflow` directly) that fans the detected agents out as a `pipeline`, then adversarially verifies each finding before aggregation:
189-
190-```js
191:// one stage per detected agent, then a verify pass per finding (no barrier between agents)
192-const findings = await pipeline(
193-  detectedAgents,                                   // e.g. [web-audit, api-audit, ...]
194:  a => agent(a.prompt, { phase: 'Scan', schema: FINDINGS }),
195:  scan => parallel(scan.findings.map(f => () =>
196:    agent(`Adversarially verify: ${f.title}`, { phase: 'Verify', schema: VERDICT })
197-      .then(v => ({ ...f, verdict: v }))))
198-)
199-```
200-
201:Benefits: background execution across tens-to-hundreds of agents, built-in worktree isolation per stage, and per-finding adversarial verification that drops false positives before they reach the SARIF report. The manual Step 2 dispatch (`run_in_background` + Monitor) remains the fallback for small projects or when a deterministic script is overkill.
202-
203-### Step 3: Collect & Parse Results
204-
205:Wait for all agents to complete. For each agent result:
206-
207:1. **Extract JSON**: Parse the agent's response to find the JSON code block (between ` ```json ` and ` ``` ` or `[` to `]`)
208-2. **Validate findings against schema**: Each finding MUST conform to this JSON schema — reject any finding missing required fields:
209-   - **Required**: `id` (string), `severity` (CRITICAL|HIGH|MEDIUM|LOW|INFO), `title` (string), `description` (string), `location.file` (string), `remediation` (string)
210-   - **Optional**: `location.line`, `location.column`, `standard`, `owasp`, `cwe`, `cvss_v4` (number 0-10), `epss` (number 0-1)
211-   - Discard findings that don't match (log which ones were rejected and why)
212:3. **Fallback**: If an agent does not return valid JSON:
213:   - Log a warning: `"WARNING: Agent {agent_name} did not return valid Finding[] JSON — skipping"`
214:   - Continue with remaining agents — do NOT fail the entire audit
215:4. **Tag findings**: Add the originating agent name to each finding for traceability
216:5. **Track agent success**: Count successful vs failed agents for the report summary
217-
218-**Edge cases:**
219:- **0 agents dispatched** (only defaults run): Proceed with `supply-chain-audit` and `data-privacy-audit` only. Add a note in the report: "No stack-specific agents detected — only default agents ran."
220:- **All agents fail**: Generate a minimal error report with 0 findings, listing which agents failed and why. Do NOT return an empty response — always produce a report.
221-
222-### Step 4: Aggregate & Score
223-
224:1. **Merge** all agent findings into a unified array
225-2. **Deduplicate** findings by `location.file` + `location.line` + `id` — keep the finding with the higher `cvss_v4` score
226-3. **Calculate risk scores**:
227:   - **CVSS v4** base score from the finding (set by agent from KB enrichment)
228:   - **EPSS** probability if CVE is mapped (set by agent from KB enrichment)
229-   - **Composite risk** = `cvss_v4 * (0.6 + 0.4 * epss)` — EPSS boosts score up to 40% max (see `risk-scorer.ts`)
230-4. **Sort** findings by composite risk (highest first)
231-
232-### Step 5: Generate Report
233-
234:Use the report renderer (`report-renderer.ts`) with the template at `/Users/manuelturpin/.sentinel/reports/templates/full-report.md`:
235-
236:1. Build a `ReportData` object from the aggregated findings, scan metadata (stacks, agents, depth, duration), and file paths
237:2. Include agent success summary: "X of Y agents completed successfully" in the report header
238-3. Call `renderReport(data)` to produce the final Markdown report
239-4. The renderer handles severity counts, composite scores, EPSS averages, and finding categorization automatically
240-
241-### Step 6: Save Reports
242-
243:Save all 3 output files to `/Users/manuelturpin/.sentinel/reports/archive/`:
244-
245:1. `{project}_{date}.sarif.json` — SARIF 2.1.0 report (with `invocations` and `artifacts`)
246-2. `{project}_{date}.sbom.json` — CycloneDX 1.5 SBOM (from `generate-sbom` tool)
247-3. `{project}_{date}.md` — Rendered Markdown report
